<title>USA: Almont CS, Mich., won by Comerica Securities.</title>
<headline>Almont CS, Mich., won by Comerica Securities.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Comerica Securities said it won $12.195 million of Almont Community Schools, Mich., general obligation 1996 school building and site bonds, with a net interest cost of 5.650 percent.</p>
<p>AMT: 12,195,000     DATE: 10/28/96	NYC Time: 1500	CUSIP: 020380</p>
<p>ISSUER: Almont Comm Schools					   ST: MI</p>
<p>ISSUE: GO 1996 school bldg &amp; Site				   TAX STAT:Exempt-ULT</p>
<p>M/SP/F: Aa/NA/NA							  BOOK ENTRY: Y</p>
<p>ENHANCEMENTS: FGIC Aaa/AAA/NA					 BANK QUAL: N</p>
<p>DTD: 11/01/96							     SURE BID: Y</p>
<p>DUE: 5/1/97-26						SR MGR: Comerica Securities</p>
<p>1ST CPN: 05/01/97					   DOLLAR BID: NA</p>
<p>CALL: 5/1/06 @ par					  NIC 5.650</p>
<p>DELIVERY: 45 days					   ORDERS: 5 PM EST</p>
<p>PAYING AGENT: Michigan National Bank, Farmington Hill</p>
<p>L.O.: Collins &amp; Blaha, Southfield</p>
